ry","decision_margin":-0.3137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: branch 2 handles 'timeouts and backend-specific errors' identically via a degraded marker","Out of scope explicitly excludes 'retrying across backends', so no retry recovers a transient timeout","The plan describes behavior ('return empty list', 'return degraded marker') but uses no explicit disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) for either arm","Prior behavior classified DDGSException as non-retryable NEEDS_INVESTIGATION; the fix makes ALL DDGSException non-fatal-but-non-retryable degraded"],"finding":"The wrapper's branch 2 (any non-'No results found.' DDGSException) treats every non-empty failure — including a transient timeout that was retryable/WAIT_AND_RETRY-shaped before this change — as a single non-retryable degraded marker, without stating the disposition per arm in explicit terms. A genuinely transient web outage is now permanently downgraded to 'prior art could not be verified' with no retry, and the plan never states that this is a deliberate collapse of transient→permanent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc53bc965b5b1cd8f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (decided), branch 2: 'Any other message, including timeouts and backend-specific errors - return an explicit degraded marker result'","norm_id":"n16aee1a90529c650","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A real DuckDuckGo/backend timeout during T1: rebar now reports 'prior art could not be verified' and closes the review, when a retry might have succeeded and let T1 actually assert prior-art coverage"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short 'Failure-disposition contract' note: branch 1 surfaces a benign empty result; branch 2 surfaces a NON-RETRYABLE degraded marker, and explicitly acknowledge that transient/timeout failures are deliberately treated as non-retryable here (retry deferred to the out-of-scope backend-retry work) so a read